    {
      "data": {
        "text": "<thinking> To create the Python file `redact_unsafe.py` that flags or redacts unsafe spans from text using an external provider, I will choose Amazon Comprehend as the concrete external provider. Amazon Comprehend is a natural language processing (NLP) service that uses machine learning to find insights and relationships in text. It can be used to detect unsafe content such as profanity, violence, and sexually explicit content. I will import the necessary modules from the `boto3` library, which is the Amazon Web Services (AWS) SDK for Python, to interact with Amazon Comprehend. The provider will be identifiable by the import of `boto3` and the use of the `comprehend` client. </thinking>\n",
        "time": {
          "end": 1789887648790,
          "start": 1789887646589
        },
        "type": "text"
      },
